BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Little Gather | Allegany River Seneca Dancers
DTSTART:20260812T133000Z
DTEND:20260812T160000Z
DTSTAMP:20260809T201414Z
UID:d5d6c9edaaa93e33390279cb4d63e32f9f8ad46d@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Education,Family Fun,Performing Arts,Dancing,History & Heritage
DESCRIPTION:August 12\, 2026 9:30 am–12:00 pm EDT\nAuditorium\nExperienc
 e the energy\, beauty\, and tradition of live music and dance as we celebr
 ate the 25th anniversary of Little Gather during our Summer of Wonder with
  the Allegany River Seneca Dancers!\nThrough traditional songs\, dances\, 
 live music\, and cultural storytelling\, the Allegany River Seneca Dancers
  share the richness of Seneca language and culture in a performance that i
 s both educational and entertaining. Audiences will learn about the origin
 s of featured songs and dances while enjoying the movement\, music\, and v
 ibrant regalia that make this experience so special. The performance may a
 lso include the Iroquois Smoke Dance\, a fast-paced contest dance that is 
 always exciting to see.\nPerforming at colleges\, museums\, powwows\, and 
 festivals since the mid-1980s\, the Allegany River Seneca Dancers offer an
  engaging and memorable experience for audiences of all ages. This perform
 ance also offers a meaningful connection to CMoG’s installation\, Glass 
 in the Hodi:nohšö:nih Confederacy\, which centers Seneca perspectives an
 d voices.\nThis program is perfect for youngsters aged 11 and under\, but 
 everyone is welcome and encouraged to attend!\nSchedule\nGroups Only: 9:30
  am–10:30 am (Reservations Required)\nGeneral Public Performance: 11 am
 –12 pm\nGroups can email littlegather@cmog.org to reserve a spot.\nBonus
  Fun\nOur friends from The Southeast Steuben County Library will also be o
 n-site with at-home activity ideas for families to enjoy. After the perfor
 mance\, the fun continues across the Museum! During your visit\, you can e
 njoy:\nscavenger hunts and themed coloring sheets inspired by the performa
 nce\na special themed glassmaking demonstration at 12:45 pm in the Amphith
 eater Hot Shop\nhands-on experiences with Guides in the Galleries\nthemed 
 treats available for purchase in the Café\nEnjoy the Museum—for Free!\n
 After the performance\, Little Gather guests and their accompanying adults
  can enjoy free admission to the Museum. Just check in at either the Audit
 orium desk or the Admissions desk\, no coupon required. Adults must be acc
 ompanied by kids to receive this offer. As always\, kids and teens 17 and 
 under are free.\nCome celebrate 25 years of Little Gather with us and enjo
 y a morning filled with music\, movement\, culture\, discovery\, and summe
 r fun!\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78
 416471/20260812093000
GEO:42.1498;77.0542
LOCATION:Corning Museum of Glass\, One Museum Way\, Corning\, NY\, 14830
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78416471/20260812093000
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wild Wednesday at Tanglewood - Migration Madness
DTSTART:20260812T140000Z
DTEND:20260813T035959Z
DTSTAMP:20260809T201414Z
UID:7dea31e9fa7d5c31fe667be3626b0a336c573a1a@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Nature,Connection,Family Fun
DESCRIPTION:What animals migrate? The answer may surprise you! Join us for
  a fun and informative program all about the species that migrate and the 
 reasons behind their incredible journeys. We’ll meet some of our animal 
 ambassadors who could migrate in the wild\, then take a short walk through
  our pollinator garden and around the pond to look for migrating butterfli
 es or birds. Feel free to bring your own binoculars if you’d like to do 
 some birdwatching!\nRegistration is appreciated\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - h
 ttps://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78433524/20260812100000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78433524/20260812100000
